    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0812" n="722" xml:id="pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/349: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McMillin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-02-26T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 26,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>12. Your February 21, 6 P.M.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d616-f1"/> While the situation
                    in Guatemala requires the closest attention the Department desires to hold
                    itself completely aloof from any action that might be construed as indicating
                    that this Government was taking any position in what is for the present a purely
                    domestic matter. In dealing with the present situation you will be guided by the
                    attitude of this Government as expressed above.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
